      "notes": [
        "The two signed measurements are the same envelope on the same route from the same key. They differ by exactly one step: the first is claimed and fsynced before the handler refuses it, the second is caught by the in-memory replay set at the claim and never written.",
        "Verification and the quota charge cost 0.27ms against 0.20ms for the durable replay claim -- within 3x of each other, so neither dominates and this run supports no claim about the ordering. Storage whose fsync is nearly free (a CI runner, a cached virtual disk) reads like this, and the ordering flips between runs on the same machine. Read this drill on hardware with the durability characteristics you intend to deploy on; §6.3's conclusion was drawn where the claim costs about 23x the verify."
